All visual assets and brand tooling identified as Kabuqina brand assets in this
repository, including but not limited to:

- The Kabuqina / 卡布奇娜 name, wordmarks, and logos (kabuqina_qi_*)
- The coffee-cup mascot and derivative exports (kabuqina_mascot*, mascot_*)
- Scene and coaster vector composites (kabuqina_hero_scene.svg,
  kabuqina_pill_scene.svg, kabuqina_coaster_hero.svg, kabuqina_coaster_pill.svg,
  kabuqina_social_preview.svg, and related exports)
- Product icons, favicons, social preview images, and app icon sets generated
  from brand sources (historical tauri/icons/ contents, and the real icon sets
  injected during official branded builds)
- Vector masters (e.g. kabuqina_mascot.svg) and raster distribution copies —
  now maintained in the private Kabuqina/kabuqina-mascot repository; their
  historical copies under Na_logo/ and web/public/ in this repository's git
  history remain covered
- Brand asset generator scripts (generate_mascot.py,
  generate_mascot_scenes.py, generate_na_mark.py) — now in the private
  repository's masters/ tree; historical copies under Na_logo/ remain
  covered, including their geometry, palette definitions, export parameters,
  and generated output

are proprietary and protected by copyright and trademark law.

Coverage rule (in addition to the illustrative list above):

1. ALL files under assets/brand/ and assets/ui/ are covered, EXCEPT
   assets/brand/placeholder/: that directory contains neutral, unbranded
   placeholder tooling and output licensed under Apache-2.0, and neither it
   nor the placeholder assets it writes into build paths (web/public/,
   tauri/icons/) are Kabuqina brand artwork.
2. The retired Na_logo/ tree is covered wherever it appears in this
   repository's git history. Its authoritative masters now live in the
   private Kabuqina/kabuqina-mascot repository, which is covered in its
   entirety.
3. ANY file in this repository bearing the SPDX identifier
   "LicenseRef-Kabuqina-Brand" (alone or in an SPDX expression such as
   "Apache-2.0 AND LicenseRef-Kabuqina-Brand") is covered to the extent
   stated in that file's header.
4. The Kabuqina brand ARTWORK — the mascot design, vector geometry, palette
   definitions, and scene compositions — is covered AS A WORK regardless of
   the file format or location in which it is expressed. This includes
   inline-vector and CSS renderings embedded in source-code files (for
   example under web/src/components/), historical copies in build paths,
   and the real assets injected into build paths during official branded
   builds, even where the surrounding component CODE is licensed under
   Apache-2.0. In such mixed files the code license grants no rights to the
   embedded artwork.

They are NOT covered by the Apache License, Version 2.0 governing the Kabuqina
source code in this repository. See the root LICENSE file and BRAND.md for the
split. Unbranded forks are welcome to replace the artwork data (geometry,
palette, mascot) with their own; the surrounding Apache-2.0 component code may
be reused for that purpose.

You may NOT use, reproduce, modify, or distribute these brand assets or generator
scripts without prior written permission, except as required to run an unmodified
copy of the official Kabuqina application binary you obtained from an authorized
source.

